    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe requirement was to re-base date-derived values onto a fiscal year that starts **1 July**, exposing a new `fiscalYear` field (`FY<YY>`) and making both the membership identifier's year segment and the tenure calculation use it.\n\n**New `util/FiscalYear.java`** \u2014 a small, single-responsibility utility that owns all fiscal-year logic, mirroring the existing `BusinessDay` utility:\n- `of(date)` \u2014 the fiscal year containing a date, identified by the calendar year it ends in (dates \u2265 1 July belong to the next year's FY). This follows the Australian convention the app already uses (NSW/VIC/QLD, `Australia/*` timezones).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 the `\"FY<YY>\"` string.\n- `yearsBetween(start, end)` \u2014 elapsed fiscal years (1 July boundaries crossed).\n\n**`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced the day-based `getTenureDays()` with:\n- `getFiscalYear()` \u2192 `FiscalYear.label(registrationDate)` (the registration date is already business-day-adjusted at `@PrePersist`, so this satisfies \"derived from the business-day-adjusted registration date\").\n- `getTenureFiscalYears()` \u2192 elapsed fiscal years. Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**:\n- Added the `fiscalYear` mapping.\n- `formatMembershipNumber` now derives `M<YY>` by reusing `owner.getFiscalYear()` (so the identifier's year segment and the `fiscalYear` field can never disagree), instead of `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`.\n- Membership points now key off `getTenureFiscalYears() > 1` (constant renamed `TENURE_POINTS_THRESHOLD_FISCAL_YEARS`), replacing the old `> 365` days window.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` schema property and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to match the new fiscal-year basis.\n\nEach concern stays in its natural home: the calendar arithmetic in a util, the entity-level derivations on `Owner`, and the DTO shaping in the mapper \u2014 with no duplication of the fiscal-year rule.\n\nThe behaviour change is intentional per the spec: e.g. an owner registered 2026-09-17 now reports `fiscalYear=FY27` and `membershipNumber=\u2026-M27` (September falls in the FY ending 2027), as seen in the audit log during the test run.",
